The 'styles/hud' folder holds the CSS modules for the opt-in compact HUD layout's React components (apps/game-client/src/components/hud/), introduced by the 2026-09-14 custom-hud-layout plan. It establishes the baseline/untheme visual look for the compact shell (terminal panel with an embedded title via the shared borderedPanelTitle mixin, vitals gauges, room row, plugin widget slots) while exposing plain `sa-hud-*` global class hooks on the rendered elements so an opt-in theme (public/themes/slate-amber.css, loaded via features/hudLayout/hudThemeLoader.ts) can repaint them without depending on Vite's hashed CSS-module class names. Per the design spec (§4.3), the baseline module always owns a working default appearance — a theme only ever layers on top, never supplies the only color.
